<title>UK: Bank of Cyprus prices 40 million Cyprus pound bond.</title>
<headline>Bank of Cyprus prices 40 million Cyprus pound bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus Ltd has priced a convertible bond of 40 million Cyrpus pounds announced on October 21 via led manager Salomon Brothers International.</p>
<p>The deal has a seven-year maturity with a call after three years and is subject to a 130 percent hurdle thereafter.</p>
<p>It will pay an annual coupon of 6.75 percent. The conversion premium is 15 percent.</p>
<p> AMT *C40 MLN	  COUPON     6.75 PCT  MATURITY    31.OCT.03</p>
<p> TYPE CONVERTIBLE     ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    31.OCT.96</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) ONE (REGS) 100 (144A)</p>
<p> MGT/UND    1.0 PCT   SELL CONC  1.50 PCT</p>
<p> NOTES	*INCLUDING FIVE MILLION CYPRUS POUND GREENSHOE</p>
<p>-- LONDON NEWSROOM +44 171 542 7658</p>
